+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering a change to pickup reminders. Reminders go by SMS because an email trial saw more
+missed pickups and fresh food thrown away. This page preserves the evidence after repeated proposals to save the
+SMS cost.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+During the April–June 2025 email trial, the provider reported that 34% of reminder emails were never opened.
+Missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup left a packed bag, with its fresh food
+going in the bin by closing time. The pantry lead reported that many members share one phone in the family and
+never check email, but do see SMS.
+
+Reminders switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August. When email was
+proposed again in [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md), the maintainer confirmed that reminders would stay on SMS.
+
+Email was proposed because it is free, while SMS cost €40 a month at the time of that discussion. The team accepts
+that SMS expense to reach members and reduce missed pickups and wasted fresh food. The email trial's outcome is
+why the saving alone did not justify switching.
+
+## Implementation
+
+The reminder timing, message and channel selection live in [the reminder code](../../larder/reminders.py).
